## README.md (deployment instructions)

```md
# Equirain — GitHub Pages Deployment

## 1) Create GitHub repo
- Create a new repository named `YOUR_USERNAME.github.io` (replace YOUR_USERNAME with your GitHub username)
- Example: `harshgill.github.io`

## 2) Upload files
- Upload `index.html` and `style.css` to the repository root
- Commit changes

## 3) Enable GitHub Pages
- Settings → Pages → Source: `main` branch (or `gh-pages`) and `/ (root)` folder → Save
- Your site will be available at `https://YOUR_USERNAME.github.io`

## 4) (Optional) Add custom domain `equirain.io`
**Important:** you must first buy `equirain.io` from a registrar (examples below).

### DNS setup for apex domain (equirain.io):
Add these **A** records for `@` (apex):
- 185.199.108.153
- 185.199.109.153
- 185.199.110.153
- 185.199.111.153

Add this **CNAME** for `www`:
- Name: `www`
- Value: `YOUR_USERNAME.github.io.`

After DNS changes, in your GitHub Pages settings add `equirain.io` as the custom domain and verify. GitHub will also prompt you to add a TXT record for verification if needed.

## 5) Email
- After you buy the domain, you can set up email (MX records) with your registrar or a provider.

## 6) Notes & security
- GitHub provides free HTTPS (SSL) for custom domains — it can take up to an hour to issue certificate after DNS is correct.
- Keep a copy of your repository and backup private data elsewhere.
```

